From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:52:20 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: mock Neo media devices with native no-grant bindings

Expose Window-only, secure-context MediaDevices, MediaDeviceInfo and
InputDeviceInfo using native Zig/V8 bindings. Model the MacBook Neo's
logical microphone, camera and speaker endpoints without consulting host
hardware. Return fresh anonymized device objects; hide labels, IDs and
input capabilities before any capture grant.

Match the ordinary Chrome prototype surface: enumerateDevices,
getSupportedConstraints, getUserMedia, getDisplayMedia,
setCaptureHandleConfig and ondevicechange. Capture requests are validated
and refused, never resolved to nonexistent streams. Interpret the media
permissions-policy directives for enumeration and screen-capture
delegation; do not introduce a general policy API or successful capture.

Preserve Navigator singleton identity, device branding and inheritance,
secure exposure across origin changes, native receiver checks, dictionary
conversion order, IteratorClose and EventTarget listener behavior.
Populate sequence results with own data properties. Use weak finalizers
for disposable device chains, page-backed escaping DOMExceptions and
Promise settlement without a mid-script microtask checkpoint.

Scope: static no-capture-grant persona, not permission UI, host enumeration,
hot-plug events, actual streams or a configurable hardware backend.
Explicit capture grants through CDP are not modeled by this API.
Reference API shape uses pinned Chromium 155.0.8053.0 Blink IDL/source,
with Chrome 154 Linux observations for engine-level descriptors; an
actual Mac Chrome reference was not available. Hardware follows AGENTS.md.

References:
https://w3c.github.io/mediacapture-main/
https://w3c.github.io/mediacapture-screen-share/
https://w3c.github.io/mediacapture-handle/identity/
https://github.com/chromium/chromium/tree/155.0.8053.0/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/mediastream
https://www.apple.com/macbook-neo/specs/

Validation before export: existing upstream suite 1658/1658; temporary
native API diagnostics 91/91; matching diagnostic-only GC snapshot 92/92,
including collectible enumeration devices and retained metadata/errors.
No new persistent unit tests or benchmark assertions.
